{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The Echo Show 5 feels like a useful next choice because a small Alexa display could add home controls and access to compatible camera feeds alongside my Fire TV and security devices.",
    "The Echo Dot and HDMI cable connect to my interest in home entertainment and connected devices, although neither fills an immediate need for me."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The older and HD Fire TV sticks repeat functions I already have with my 4K stick and Fire TV television, without offering a clear improvement.",
    "The earbuds and older tablet do not address my current home video and security interests, while the memory cards and Wi-Fi extender require a storage or coverage need I have not established."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My Fire TV purchases seem to have been taken as a reason to recommend more Fire TV devices, even when they duplicate what I already use.",
    "Owning electronics seems to have been treated as interest in general accessories, even though a memory card or network extender needs a specific purpose."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "What matters to me is whether a device adds a useful capability to my existing setup; another streaming stick is less compelling than a display that could help me interact with compatible cameras.",
    "A related item is not automatically something I would choose now: I need a concrete use for another cable, storage card, or networking device."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my interest in connected home video devices but miss the difference between adding a useful capability and duplicating equipment I already have."
}"}
